WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.734
-It is so great to see you.
Welcome to the show.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.033
-It's surreal actually
being on this side of it.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.601
It's so fabulous. I love it.
-Oh, yeah. Were we Zooming?

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.567
-I'm a fan.
I just watch it all the time.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:11.567
-Oh, stop.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:12.968
Well, we've talked about
your show,

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.367
"Mary McCartney Serves It Up."

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:15.734
It was nominated for an Emmy,
by the way.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.100
Congratulations.
-Yes, thank you.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.133
-You do that. You host.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.901
You're an amazing photographer,
by the way.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.868
-This documentary,
"If These Walls Could Sing,"

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.033
was nominated
for a Critics' Choice Award.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.067
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah. That was surreal.

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.334
-Well, look at you,
who's getting --

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.667
You're just getting
nominated left and right.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.701
-Do you know what won?
Do you know what beat me?

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:33.968
-No.
-"Get Back."

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.400
-Oh, my gosh. Hilarious.
So your dad's documentary?

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.567
-I was happy with that.
-Yeah, exactly. I guess so.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:41.434
Yeah. But when they offer
you this documentary and --

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.434
or it comes to -- I don't know
if you thought of the idea,

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:46.801
or do you go like, "It's
90 years of Abbey Road Studios."

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.300
-No. It was brought to me.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.100
The producer, John Battsek,
who's, like,

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.934
an Oscar-winning
documentary director --

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.400
he texted me and he was like,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.300
"Have you thought of
directing documentaries?"

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.968
And as a photographer, it's kind
of a natural progression

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.267
to go into directing,
so I was like, "Yeah."

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:06.000
He said he was doing a
documentary about Abbey Road,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.934
"90 years of Abbey Road."

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.200
I had no idea that Abbey Road
was 90 years old.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.334
-Yeah.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:12.667
-The reason I
really wanted to do it was

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.767
a funny reason, as well,
was there's a picture

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:18.000
that I saw in a book
in Abbey Road

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.667
of my mom leading a pony across
the zebra crossing in the '70s.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.367
Oh, you -- Yeah.
-I have this.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.601
-It's in the documentary.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:28.901
This picture is --
It was sort of like,

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.801
"Well, I'm destined to do
this documentary,

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.234
really, aren't I, if that's --"

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.367
-How did they get a pony --
Why is a pony going across --

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.901
-That's just like my mom.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:38.801
She loved horses and animals
and she was going to work

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.667
and she's like, "Let's take --"
The pony's called Jet.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.634
She was like,
"Let's take Jet to work."

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.067
-So you're just gonna take
a pony to work. Why not?

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.734
-And as dad says
in the documentary --

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:47.734
I kind of bring this in.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.100
This is in the beginning.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.434
He says, "I don't think
he disgraced himself either."

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.801
-Yeah. No, he is fantastic.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:57.167
And, also, it's like Pink Floyd,
"Dark Side of the Moon"

00:01:57.167 --> 00:02:00.968
was recorded there, all of
the -- Like, all of the --

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.534
John Williams I interview.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.334
All of, like, "Indiana Jones."

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:07.334
Because Studio One
is the big classical space.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.200
And that was
in danger of closing down

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.901
because all of the
main classical recordings

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.234
had done,
and business was drying up.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.634
So, they were using it as,
like, a badminton court.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.300
Like, it was empty and vast.
-Is that right?

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.033
And they were looking at
making it into a car park.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.968
And then the manager,
Ken Townsend,

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.968
found out that a studio
was closing.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.534
A film studio in Denham
had lost its lease.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:28.934
He brought in the contract

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.701
and quickly put a projector in
and a screen.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.567
And one of
the first people there was

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:38.133
George Lucas and John Williams
doing "Indiana Jones."

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:39.534
-Is that right?
-Absolutely.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:40.968
-So, the movie kind of saved it.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.767
The movie industry saved
Abbey Road.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.434
-See, I'm such an expert now.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:47.133
-Yeah, now it -- Now you
can tell me anything about it.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.367
Yeah. Well, everyone
just called it as like,

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.834
oh, that was the nickname
of the studio?

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:55.167
-It was called it EMI Studios
'cause it's part of EMI.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.133
And then everyone
called it Abbey Road

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.167
because it's on Abbey Road.

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.400
And then the album
made it famous.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.167
And then, Ken Townsend --
It didn't change the name

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.334
until 1976.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:05.834
-After the album.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:08.667
-And you actually brought us a
sketch that your dad made of --

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.200
This is pretty awesome.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.267
-So, in the documentary,
I interviewed Ringo,

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:16.234
and he was like, "Oh, you know,
we were thinking of going --"

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:17.767
Because the engineer had

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:20.234
a packet of cigarettes
called Everest.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:21.934
So they were like,
"Oh, should we go to

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.434
the top of Everest and do a
photo shoot, call it 'Everest,'

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:26.334
or should we go to,
you know, Hawaii --"

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:28.100
-Yes, the final --
It's The Beatles' album.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.767
"Everest" is the last album.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.000
And then they were like, "No,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.767
let's just go onto the
zebra crossing."

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.767
And dad drew this,
sketched out this picture,

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:39.334
which is kind of very close to
pretty much what it did.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.100
This one up here, I think.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.734
-Yeah.
-I mean, yeah.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:47.133
It ended up being the most fun.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.868
-I mean, that's basically --
That's the sketch.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.868
-It's a great picture.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.934
-That's the sketch.
-Yeah. I know.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.501
It's good, right?
-That's unbelievable, yeah.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.801
-Yeah.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.467
-And you obviously got to
interview your dad for this.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.901
-Mm-hmm.
-Was that awkward for you?

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:04.701
-They all -- Dad included,
they all kind of came --

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.133
A lot of them I interviewed in
Abbey Road, in the studio,

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:08.434
so they felt the feeling.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:11.000
It's, like, this feeling of
warmth and inspiration

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.300
when you go in there.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.067
So, they all brought their game.

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:16.300
But there was a cute moment when
I was sitting with dad,

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.667
and I was, like, talking.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.834
I was really well-researched and
being really professional,

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:22.133
and he kind of glazed over
and he was like,

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.434
"Oh, that's my daughter.

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:25.767
You're like a
female director directing me."

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.234
And I was like,
"Get back to work."

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:31.067
-Yeah, yeah.
"Let's go to the studio." Yeah.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.300
It's really fascinating.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.234
This is
"If These Walls Could Sing."

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:36.667
Take a look at this.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:40.000
-I remember playing on a
Barron Knights session here,

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.033
and "Hey Jude"
had just come out.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:46.634
So, I was standing with Bernie,
and your dad came in the door

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:47.834
and said "hello"
to The Barron Knights.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.033
And that was the first time

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.667
I'd ever seen anyone
that famous in my life.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.868
And I kind of froze,
and Bernie did, too.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.734
And The Barron Knights
asked Paul to play

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.434
"Hey Jude" on the piano,
and he did.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.334
And Bernie and I
have never forgotten it.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.767
It's like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.467
We saw Paul play 'Hey Jude'
at time the record came out."

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.467
-Come on.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:09.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Mary McCartney.

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:10.968
"If These Walls Could Sing"

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:14.334
premieres December 16th
on Disney+.

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:15.767
We'll be right back with
a performance from

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:16.801
Adam Blackstone.

